# Uldaros Theorix and a double-faced card (CR 712.8a, 712.11): a double-faced card in exile has the characteristics of its front face
# only, so Aang, Swift Savior (a creature, mana value 3) counts 3 towards the six and is cast, front face up, as a copy that
# becomes a token. Bot1 exiles Aang, The Theorist, Jace Beleren (4) and the sacrificed Black Lotus (0): after Aang, 3 is left, so
# Jace is not castable and is not offered, but the Lotus is. (This engine has no modal double-faced card among its cards: this is the
# transforming one, whose back face cannot be cast.)

